// expect-ok
// Z3 corpus #80: PR-U3-b2 — wide-BOUND refinement SATISFIED over a u256 field.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// The expect-ok half of #79 and the UP3 accept-path witness: a wide cap
// (`amount <= 10^29`, a LiteralWide bound) is satisfied by the supplied value 5,
// so Z3 proves not(5 <= 10^29) is Unsat → Holds → clean compile. The workload
// snapshot drives the production refinement_value_for + check_refinement path.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Changing `5` to a literal > 10^29 flips this to a T210 reject. Removing the
// `where` clause drops the obligation entirely.
module sigil;

record Cap { amount: u256 } where amount <= 100000000000000000000000000000

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let c: Cap = Cap { amount: 5 };
        return 1;
    }
}
